---
layout: base.njk
title: "Compare CDC Platforms"
description: "Head-to-head comparison of six CDC platforms — Debezium, AWS DMS, Fivetran, Airbyte, Oracle GoldenGate, and Qlik Replicate — on deployment, method, delivery semantics, latency, and cost."
canonicalPath: "/compare/"
---
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}

{{ ui.hero(heroConfig) | safe }}

<div class="page-wrap prose">
  <aside class="compare-note" role="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Read the "delivery semantics" row first.</strong> Every platform
      here delivers <strong>at-least-once</strong> at the wire — none give
      end-to-end exactly-once across systems, whatever the marketing says.
      Correctness comes from an <strong>idempotent sink</strong>: upsert on the
      primary key, ordered by the source log position (LSN/SCN), not
      <code>ts_ms</code>. Where a vendor markets "exactly-once", the table
      states the honest version.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section id="matrix" aria-labelledby="matrix-title">
    <h2 id="matrix-title">The comparison matrix</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Order-of-magnitude guidance, not benchmarks — latency, cost, and feature
      support vary with data volume, region, and configuration. Verify against
      current vendor docs.
    </p>
    <div class="compare-matrix-wrap">
      <table class="compare-matrix">
        <caption class="sr-only">CDC platforms compared across {{ cdcCompare.dimensions | length }} dimensions</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Dimension</th>
            {% for p in cdcCompare.platforms %}
              <th scope="col"><a href="#{{ p.slug }}">{{ p.name }}</a></th>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for d in cdcCompare.dimensions %}
            <tr{% if d.key == 'delivery' %} class="is-highlight"{% endif %}>
              <th scope="row">{{ d.label }}</th>
              {% for p in cdcCompare.platforms %}
                <td>{{ p[d.key] }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="platforms" aria-labelledby="platforms-title">
    <h2 id="platforms-title">Platform by platform</h2>
    <div class="compare-cards">
      {% for p in cdcCompare.platforms %}
        <article class="compare-card" id="{{ p.slug }}">
          <h3>{{ p.name }}</h3>
          <p class="compare-card__best"><strong>Best for:</strong> {{ p.bestFor }}</p>
          <div class="compare-card__cols">
            <div class="compare-card__col">
              <h4>Strengths</h4>
              <ul>
                {% for s in p.strengths %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="compare-card__col">
              <h4>Trade-offs</h4>
              <ul>
                {% for t in p.tradeoffs %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="decide" aria-labelledby="decide-title">
    <h2 id="decide-title">Decision guide</h2>
    <p>Start from the constraint that actually binds you:</p>
    <ul class="compare-decide">
      <li><strong>Zero ops, warehouse target</strong> → <a href="#fivetran">Fivetran</a> (or <a href="#airbyte">Airbyte Cloud</a>) — hand it off, dedupe in the destination MERGE.</li>
      <li><strong>All-in on AWS</strong> → <a href="#aws-dms">AWS DMS</a> — managed, IaC-friendly, into S3/Redshift/Kinesis.</li>
      <li><strong>Sub-second, full control, event-driven</strong> → <a href="#debezium">Debezium + Kafka Connect</a> — you run it, you own it.</li>
      <li><strong>Open source + broad connectors, minutes are fine</strong> → <a href="#airbyte">Airbyte</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Enterprise Oracle, heterogeneous or active-active</strong> → <a href="#goldengate">Oracle GoldenGate</a> — with the honest delivery caveat.</li>
      <li><strong>Broad connectivity, low-code / GUI-first</strong> → <a href="#qlik-replicate">Qlik Replicate</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="compare-note compare-note--tight" role="note">
      <p>
        Whatever you pick, design the sink to be idempotent. The platform choice
        changes ops, cost, and latency — it does not remove the need to dedupe
        on the primary key by log position.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="compare-related" aria-labelledby="related-title">
    <h2 id="related-title">Go deeper</h2>
    <div class="compare-related__grid">
      <a class="compare-related__card" href="{{ '/cloud-labs/' | url }}">
        <h3>Cloud labs</h3>
        <p>Hands-on walkthroughs for AWS DMS, Fivetran, GoldenGate, Matillion, and Snowflake.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="compare-related__card" href="{{ '/lab-kafka-debezium/' | url }}">
        <h3>Kafka + Debezium lab</h3>
        <p>Stand up open-source, log-based CDC end to end.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="compare-related__card" href="{{ '/tooling/' | url }}">
        <h3>Tooling &amp; versions</h3>
        <p>The full platform catalog and current version matrix.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="compare-related__card" href="{{ '/exactly-once/' | url }}">
        <h3>Exactly-once, honestly</h3>
        <p>Why delivery is at-least-once and idempotent sinks carry correctness.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
